outcome:
The verification_record sender's tick (src/engram_verification_record.rs, from w-decd61d62831) does bounded work per pass:
- registrations whose host ack is Settled or Rejected are skipped inside the locked selection;
- runs in a terminal-pending state (PostRunNotClean, UnclassifiedStages, StartedBeforeRegistration, RootGenerationOutOfRange, BodyMismatch, BodyNotBuilt, CapabilityUnsupported, InitiatingSessionGone) back off, or wait for a state change, instead of re-reading request.json, results.json and the body and rebuilding every 2 s;
- after a RoutingTokenRefused, it doesn't send another SessionStatus with the same refused token until the session's token changes.
Tests show the bounded behaviour. Provenance: w-decd review round 3 Low L10 (Claude delegation a7f9d7d4) and round 4 Low (Claude delegation 8e895e93).
